      },
      "message": "fix(post): Haas feed words carry a decimal point\n\nhaas.cps ff() wrote a whole-number F word with no point (mm: F600;\ninch: a whole in/min value such as F2). Haas Setting 77 (Scale Integer\nF) scales an F word with no point: at its default an mm control reads\nF600 as 0.6 mm/min. ff() now puts its result through pt(), as the\nlength words do (#1836); the zero literal is \"0.\". A positive feed\nthat rounds to zero keeps its fraction, and a feed below the inch\nfour-decimal step is refused by name.\n\nThe Haas goldens are regenerated: 30 files, 658 lines, only F words.\nNew pin: crates/post/tests/haas_feed_decimal_point.rs.\n\nFixes #3681\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
